WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.635
TYRION LANNISTER: Look at me
and tell me what you see.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.505
What you see is a dwarf.

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:07.407
If I'd been born a peasant,

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.075
they might have left me
out in the woods to die.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:12.679
Alas, I was born
a Lannister of Casterly Rock.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:15.115
Things are expected of me.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:19.185 line:0%
I'm Dr. Ali Mattu,
cognitive behavioral therapist,

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.155 line:0%
and I'm here today
in collaboration with HBO

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:25.158 line:0%
to offer my take
on themes of mental health

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.258
<i> in their shows.</i>

00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:29.396
Never forget what you are,
the rest of the world will not.

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:32.165
Wear it like armor,

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.334
and it can never be used
to hurt you.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.570
Today, we're focusing on
depression through the lens

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.573
of Tyrion Lannister
in<i> Game of Thrones.</i>

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:44.244
♪ (MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:53.252
Anhedonia is a core symptom
of depression,

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:57.290
and it's what happens when you
no longer experience joy

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.193
or pleasure in the things
that usually gave you

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.727
<i> joy or pleasure.</i>

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.864
It zaps any motivation you have.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.666
You seem rather drunk.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.936
Drinking and lust.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.472
No man can match me
in these things.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:14.406
(GRUNTS)

00:01:14.506 --> 00:01:16.142
Usually the first thing
people do

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.344
when they might be experiencing
anhedonia,

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:22.715
is just to try more of the kind
of stuff that they enjoy,

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.517
<i> to try to feel something.</i>

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.719
But that usually doesn't work.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:31.624
What you need is to use
that anhedonia,

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.825
and try to understand

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:36.329
<i> what changes you might need
 to make in your life</i>

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.164
to get you moving
in the direction

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.565
that you want to be in.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.067
I'd given up on life,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.737
until Varys convinced me
you might be worth living for.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:49.174
You chop off my head, well,
my final days were interesting.

00:01:49.274 --> 00:01:50.409
You're going to advise me.

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:53.045
What I like to ask my patients
is,

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:56.482
to imagine your 100th birthday.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:57.249
<i> Who's there?</i>

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:01.954
<i> What stories are they sharing
 about your relationship?</i>

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:05.325
<i> About the achievements
 that you've made in your life?</i>

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.999
What I love about Tyrion is
his story's about

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:15.768
<i> connecting with
 a larger purpose,</i>

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.771
<i>doing what's best for Westeros.</i>

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.973
Owning who he is...

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.541
(CHEERING)

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:26.011
<i> ...and the unique ways
 he can help others.</i>

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:28.348
We'll never know if Tyrion
was struggling

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.882
with a mental illness.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:31.817
But whatever
he was dealing with,

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:35.354
<i> didn't get in the way
 of him being a hero.</i>

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:38.157
And that's true for all of us.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.526
<i> No matter what
 you're experiencing,</i>

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.161
<i> it doesn't have to get
 in the way</i>

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:44.931
of living the life you want
to live.

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:48.668
<i> That's my take for the day,
 I'm Dr. Mattu.</i>

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.679
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

